Changes for this port:
  plugin.toml and all files under themes/ were created for OpenIDEA by
  mapping Nebula Aura Dark, Violet and Midnight to OpenIDEA design tokens.
  Version 1.1.0 rebuilt the base/surface/elevated/overlay hierarchy.
  Version 1.2.0 introduced low-chroma neutral borders, distinct cool-grey
  hover/current/selected states and neutral type/function/punctuation colours.
  Version 1.3.0 redesigns all variants around neutral structural colours with
  pink/violet as accents only, and restores Light as an independent near-white
  design rather than a desaturated dark theme.
  Version 1.4.0 completes the 242 themeable tokens of OpenIDEA 0.1.39
  (plugin API 1.3): the four diff stripe marks, --syn-global, and the Python
  and PHP name groups; and moves the Dark, Violet and Midnight find and
  go-to-result highlights to dark backgrounds, following the Islands scheme,
  because a bright amber background left the light syntax colours unreadable.
  The plugin icons under icons/ are vector redraws of the original icon.png
  artwork from the Nebula Aura Theme repository.
  Version 1.5.0 adds Sorbet Mint, a light variant with mint surfaces sampled
  from the reference screenshot and Cosmic Sorbet Day's syntax role
  assignment; its palette, contrast calibration and mint surface hierarchy
  were designed for this plugin.
